1
00:00:13,806 --> 00:00:17,308
Cinderella

2
00:00:17,393 --> 00:00:20,853
You're as lovely as your name

3
00:00:20,938 --> 00:00:24,023
Cinderella

4
00:00:24,108 --> 00:00:28,653
You're a sunset in a frame

5
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:31,531
Though you're dressed in rags

6
00:00:31,615 --> 00:00:36,536
You wear an air of queenly grace

7
00:00:36,662 --> 00:00:38,996
Anyone can see

8
00:00:39,081 --> 00:00:44,711
A throne would be your proper place

9
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:48,047
Cinderella

10
00:00:48,132 --> 00:00:51,551
If you give your heart a chance

11
00:00:51,635 --> 00:00:54,679
It will lead you

12
00:00:54,763 --> 00:00:59,100
To the kingdom of romance

13
00:00:59,935 --> 00:01:05,398
There you'll see your dreams unfold

14
00:01:07,526 --> 00:01:14,031
Cinderella

15
00:01:14,116 --> 00:01:16,868
In the sweetest story

16
00:01:16,952 --> 00:01:21,247
Ever told

17
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:40,141
Once upon a time,
in a faraway land,

18
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:42,185
there was a tiny kingdom,

19
00:01:44,146 --> 00:01:48,149
peaceful, prosperous,
and rich in romance and tradition.

20
00:01:52,488 --> 00:01:54,489
Here, in a stately chateau,

21
00:01:54,573 --> 00:01:56,449
there lived a widowed gentleman

22
00:01:56,533 --> 00:01:58,785
and his little daughter, Cinderella.

23
00:02:01,038 --> 00:02:03,539
Although he was
a kind and devoted father,

24
00:02:03,624 --> 00:02:06,793
and gave his beloved child
every luxury and comfort,

25
00:02:06,877 --> 00:02:10,087
still, he felt she needed
a mother's care.

26
00:02:10,172 --> 00:02:11,923
And so, he married again,

27
00:02:12,007 --> 00:02:15,593
choosing for his second wife
a woman of good family,

28
00:02:15,677 --> 00:02:18,429
with two daughters
just Cinderella's age,

29
00:02:18,514 --> 00:02:21,975
by name, Anastasia and Drizella.

30
00:02:59,388 --> 00:03:02,515
Well, it serves you right,
spoiling people's best dreams.

31
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:06,268
Yes, I know it's a lovely morning,

32
00:03:06,353 --> 00:03:08,979
but it was a lovely dream, too.

33
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:15,736
What kind of a dream?

34
00:03:16,905 --> 00:03:17,988
Can't tell.

35
00:03:20,283 --> 00:03:23,953
'Cause if you tell a wish,
it won't come true.

36
00:03:24,037 --> 00:03:25,204
And, after all...

37
00:03:25,622 --> 00:03:30,167
A dream is a wish

38
00:03:30,293 --> 00:03:34,505
Your heart makes

39
00:03:34,589 --> 00:03:40,302
When you're fast asleep

40
00:03:40,387 --> 00:03:44,473
In dreams you will lose

41
00:03:44,558 --> 00:03:46,892
Your heartaches

42
00:03:48,437 --> 00:03:52,481
Whatever you wish for

43
00:03:52,566 --> 00:03:53,774
You keep

44
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:58,362
Have faith

45
00:03:58,447 --> 00:04:04,285
In your dreams and someday

46
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:11,625
Your rainbow
will come smiling through

47
00:04:12,711 --> 00:04:18,132
No matter how your heart is grieving

48
00:04:19,301 --> 00:04:23,554
If you keep on believing

49
00:04:24,765 --> 00:04:28,726
The dream that you wish

50
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:34,190
Will come true

51
00:04:35,901 --> 00:04:37,526
Oh, that clock.

52
00:04:39,154 --> 00:04:40,362
Old killjoy.

53
00:04:41,406 --> 00:04:44,033
I hear you. "Come on, get up," you say.

54
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:47,453
Time to start another day.

55
00:04:47,537 --> 00:04:49,747
Even he orders me around.

56
00:04:51,249 --> 00:04:53,125
Well, there's one thing.

57
00:04:53,210 --> 00:04:56,587
They can't order me to stop dreaming.

58
00:04:56,671 --> 00:04:59,507
And perhaps someday...

59
00:04:59,591 --> 00:05:03,427
The dreams that I wish

60
00:05:03,512 --> 00:05:08,808
Will come true

61
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:19,837
No matter how your heart is grieving

62
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:25,426
If you keep on believing

63
00:06:26,678 --> 00:06:29,930
The dream that you wish

64
00:06:30,015 --> 00:06:35,227
Will come true

65
00:06:35,312 --> 00:06:38,063
- Look what I found.
- Over there, Cinderella.

66
00:06:38,148 --> 00:06:40,190
Wait a minute.

67
00:06:40,275 --> 00:06:41,984
One at a time, please.

68
00:06:42,319 --> 00:06:44,737
Now, Jaq, what's all the fuss about?

69
00:06:44,821 --> 00:06:46,155
New mouse in the house.

70
00:06:46,239 --> 00:06:48,115
Brand-new. Never saw it before.

71
00:06:48,199 --> 00:06:50,784
- Visitor. Visitor!
- Oh, a visitor.

72
00:06:51,286 --> 00:06:53,329
Well, she'll need a dress...

73
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:56,916
- No, no, no.
- It's not a she, it's a he.

74
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,710
- He, he.
- Oh, that does make a difference.

75
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:03,714
- He'll need a jacket and shoes...
- Gotta get him out!

76
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:05,841
- It's in a rat trap.
- Where?

77
00:07:05,926 --> 00:07:08,469
In a trap? Why didn't you say so?

78
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:25,361
Now, now, calm down, everybody.

79
00:07:27,113 --> 00:07:30,199
Oh, the poor little thing's
scared to death.

80
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:33,160
Jaq, maybe you better
explain things to him.

81
00:07:33,244 --> 00:07:35,579
Zuk, zuk, Cinderelly.

82
00:07:35,664 --> 00:07:38,332
Now, now. Look, little guy.

83
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:41,168
Take it easy. Nothin' to worry about.

84
00:07:41,252 --> 00:07:43,921
We like you. Cinderelly likes you, too.

85
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:45,673
She's nice, very nice.

86
00:07:45,757 --> 00:07:49,134
That's better. Come on, now. Zuk, zuk.

87
00:07:49,219 --> 00:07:51,178
Zuk, zuk.

88
00:07:54,015 --> 00:07:55,683
Well, that's better.

89
00:07:58,353 --> 00:08:00,896
Well, let's just slip it on for size.

90
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:05,943
It is a little snug.

91
00:08:06,027 --> 00:08:07,820
But it'll have to do.

92
00:08:08,238 --> 00:08:09,863
Now, for a name.

93
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:12,784
Gus-Gus take the Lucify and look at!

94
00:08:12,868 --> 00:08:14,160
No, Gus-Gus, no.

95
00:08:14,245 --> 00:08:16,454
Now, listen here. Lucify not funny.

96
00:08:16,539 --> 00:08:18,248
Lucify mean.

97
00:08:32,721 --> 00:08:33,972
Bruno.

98
00:08:35,891 --> 00:08:37,100
Bruno!

99
00:08:44,066 --> 00:08:45,859
Dreaming again.

100
00:08:45,943 --> 00:08:48,403
Chasing Lucifer?

101
00:08:48,487 --> 00:08:51,364
Catch him this time? That's bad.

102
00:08:54,577 --> 00:08:56,661
Suppose they heard you upstairs.

103
00:08:56,745 --> 00:08:58,329
You know the orders.

104
00:08:59,081 --> 00:09:02,041
So if you don't want
to lose that nice, warm bed,

105
00:09:02,126 --> 00:09:04,669
you'd better get rid of those dreams.

106
00:09:05,254 --> 00:09:06,504
Know how?

107
00:09:08,090 --> 00:09:09,841
Just learn to like cats.

108
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:16,347
No, I mean it.
Lucifer has his good points, too.

109
00:09:16,432 --> 00:09:18,391
For one thing, he...

110
00:09:21,103 --> 00:09:24,355
Well, sometimes he...

111
00:09:26,775 --> 00:09:29,027
There must be
something good about him.

112
00:09:42,541 --> 00:09:44,375
Bruno!

113
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:46,544
Oh, Bruno.

114
00:09:46,629 --> 00:09:49,589
Come on, now. Outside.

115
00:09:52,635 --> 00:09:54,802
I know it isn't easy,

116
00:09:54,887 --> 00:09:58,056
but at least we should try
to get along together.

117
00:09:59,808 --> 00:10:02,811
And that includes you, Your Majesty.

118
00:10:10,569 --> 00:10:13,071
- Cinderella!
- I'm coming.

119
00:10:23,416 --> 00:10:25,834
- Cinderella!
- In a minute.

120
00:10:27,211 --> 00:10:43,768
Cinderella!

121
00:11:07,877 --> 00:11:11,088
My son has been avoiding his
responsibilities long enough.

122
00:11:11,172 --> 00:11:14,466
It's high time he married
and settled down.

123
00:11:15,093 --> 00:11:17,052
Of course, Your Majesty.

124
00:11:17,595 --> 00:11:18,846
But we must be patient.

125
00:11:18,930 --> 00:11:21,140
I am patient!

126
00:11:23,017 --> 00:11:26,895
But I'm not getting any younger,
you know.

127
00:11:26,980 --> 00:11:30,190
I want to see my grandchildren
before I go.

128
00:11:30,275 --> 00:11:33,026
- I understand, Sire.
- No.

129
00:11:33,111 --> 00:11:37,448
No, you don't know
what it means to see your only child

130
00:11:37,532 --> 00:11:42,411
grow farther, farther,
and farther away from you.

131
00:11:43,663 --> 00:11:44,913
I'm...

132
00:11:44,998 --> 00:11:48,125
I'm lonely in this desolate old palace.

133
00:11:48,209 --> 00:11:50,377
I... I want to hear

134
00:11:50,462 --> 00:11:53,964
the pitter-patter of little feet again.

135
00:11:55,467 --> 00:11:57,134
Now, now, Your Majesty.

136
00:11:58,678 --> 00:12:01,972
- Perhaps if we just let him alone...
- Let him alone?

137
00:12:03,349 --> 00:12:05,934
With his silly romantic ideas?

138
00:12:06,019 --> 00:12:08,896
But, Sire, in matters of love...

139
00:12:08,980 --> 00:12:10,606
Love.

140
00:12:10,690 --> 00:12:15,235
Just a boy meeting a girl
under the right conditions.

141
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:18,113
So, we're arranging the conditions.

142
00:12:18,198 --> 00:12:20,991
But, Your Majesty,
if the Prince should suspect.

143
00:12:21,075 --> 00:12:22,868
Suspect!

144
00:12:22,952 --> 00:12:25,704
Look, the boy's coming home today,
isn't he?

145
00:12:25,789 --> 00:12:26,747
Yes, Sire.

146
00:12:26,831 --> 00:12:30,959
Well, what could be more natural than a
ball to celebrate his return?

147
00:12:31,044 --> 00:12:32,920
Nothing, Sire.

148
00:12:33,004 --> 00:12:36,965
If all the eligible maidens
in my kingdom just

149
00:12:38,635 --> 00:12:40,344
happened to be there,

150
00:12:40,428 --> 00:12:44,681
why, he's bound to show interest
in one of them, isn't he?

151
00:12:44,766 --> 00:12:46,433
Isn't he?

152
00:12:46,518 --> 00:12:48,101
Yes, Sire.

153
00:12:48,186 --> 00:12:49,686
The moment he does...

154
00:12:50,605 --> 00:12:53,023
Soft lights.

155
00:12:53,107 --> 00:12:55,692
Romantic music.

156
00:12:55,777 --> 00:12:58,195
All the trimmings!

157
00:12:59,113 --> 00:13:01,031
It can't possibly fail.

158
00:13:02,116 --> 00:13:03,659
Can it?

159
00:13:04,285 --> 00:13:06,245
Yes, Sire. No, Sire!

160
00:13:06,329 --> 00:13:08,622
Very well, Sire.

161
00:13:08,706 --> 00:13:10,374
I shall arrange the ball for...

162
00:13:10,458 --> 00:13:13,001
- Tonight.
- Tonight? Tonight!

163
00:13:13,086 --> 00:13:14,711
- Oh, but, Sire...
- Tonight!

164
00:13:14,796 --> 00:13:18,257
And see that every
eligible maid is there.

165
00:13:18,341 --> 00:13:20,801
Understand?

166
00:13:22,637 --> 00:13:24,721
Yes, Your Majesty.

167
00:13:26,599 --> 00:13:28,725
The pear-shaped toad

168
00:13:31,354 --> 00:13:38,443
Sing, sweet nightingale

169
00:13:38,528 --> 00:13:41,572
High

170
00:13:41,656 --> 00:13:44,491
Above me

171
00:13:44,576 --> 00:13:48,662
Oh, sing, sweet nightingale

172
00:13:48,746 --> 00:13:51,915
Sing, sweet nightingale

173
00:13:51,1000 --> 00:13:55,919
High

174
00:13:56,004 --> 00:14:00,007
Above

175
00:14:00,091 --> 00:14:03,510
Oh, sing, sweet nightingale

176
00:14:03,595 --> 00:14:07,389
Sing, sweet nightingale

177
00:14:07,473 --> 00:14:12,769
High

178
00:14:14,939 --> 00:14:18,859
Oh, sing, sweet nightingale

179
00:14:18,943 --> 00:14:22,404
Sing, sweet

180
00:14:22,488 --> 00:14:26,199
Nightingale

181
00:14:26,284 --> 00:14:31,246
Oh, sing, sweet nightingale

182
00:14:31,331 --> 00:14:35,626
Sing, sweet

183
00:14:35,710 --> 00:14:39,922
Oh, sing, sweet nightingale

184
00:14:40,006 --> 00:14:42,674
Sing

185
00:14:44,469 --> 00:14:48,722
Oh, sing, sweet nightingale

186
00:14:48,806 --> 00:14:53,810
Oh, sing, sweet

187
00:14:54,771 --> 00:14:57,105
Oh

188
00:14:57,690 --> 00:15:00,943
Sing

189
00:15:01,903 --> 00:15:04,237
Lucifer!

190
00:15:07,158 --> 00:15:08,867
You mean old thing.

191
00:15:11,162 --> 00:15:12,996
I'm just going to have to
teach you a lesson.

192
00:15:14,874 --> 00:15:16,1000
Open in the name of the King.

193
00:15:18,586 --> 00:15:21,213
An urgent message
from His Imperial Majesty.

194
00:15:21,297 --> 00:15:23,966
- Thank you.
- From the King!

195
00:15:24,050 --> 00:15:26,176
What's it say, Cinderelly?

196
00:15:26,260 --> 00:15:27,552
What's it say, huh?

197
00:15:27,637 --> 00:15:29,096
I don't know.

198
00:15:29,180 --> 00:15:31,306
He said it's urgent.

199
00:15:33,434 --> 00:15:36,061
Maybe I should interrupt
the music lesson.

200
00:15:36,145 --> 00:15:42,234
Sing, sweet nightingale

201
00:15:42,318 --> 00:15:47,698
High

202
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:51,535
You clumsy! You did it on purpose.

203
00:15:51,911 --> 00:15:55,372
- It's her fault.
- Girls, girls. Remember,

204
00:15:55,456 --> 00:15:57,708
above all, self-control.

205
00:15:59,752 --> 00:16:00,961
Yes!

206
00:16:02,588 --> 00:16:05,132
Cinderella!
I've warned you never to interrupt...

207
00:16:05,216 --> 00:16:08,093
- This just arrived from the palace.
- From the palace!

208
00:16:08,177 --> 00:16:09,678
- Give it here.
- Let me have it.

209
00:16:10,722 --> 00:16:12,097
I'll read it.

210
00:16:12,765 --> 00:16:15,350
Well, there's to be a ball.

211
00:16:15,435 --> 00:16:18,103
- A ball!
- In honour of His Highness, the Prince.

212
00:16:18,187 --> 00:16:19,604
Oh, the Prince!

213
00:16:19,689 --> 00:16:21,898
And, by royal command,

214
00:16:21,983 --> 00:16:24,985
every eligible maiden is to attend.

215
00:16:25,069 --> 00:16:27,487
- Why, that's us!
- And I'm so eligible.

216
00:16:29,866 --> 00:16:32,325
That means I can go, too.

217
00:16:32,410 --> 00:16:35,454
Her, dancing with the Prince.

218
00:16:35,538 --> 00:16:37,706
I'd be honoured, Your Highness.

219
00:16:37,790 --> 00:16:40,542
Would you mind holding my broom?

220
00:16:43,921 --> 00:16:45,922
Well, why not?

221
00:16:47,258 --> 00:16:50,052
After all, I'm still a member of the family.

222
00:16:50,136 --> 00:16:53,013
And it says, "By royal command,

223
00:16:53,097 --> 00:16:55,807
"every eligible maiden is to attend."

224
00:16:55,892 --> 00:16:58,643
Yes, so it does.

225
00:17:00,354 --> 00:17:03,523
Well, I see no reason why you can't go.

226
00:17:03,608 --> 00:17:05,942
If you get all your work done.

227
00:17:06,027 --> 00:17:07,819
Oh, I will. I promise.

228
00:17:07,904 --> 00:17:11,490
And if you can find
something suitable to wear.

229
00:17:11,574 --> 00:17:14,035
I'm sure I can.
Oh, thank you, Stepmother.

230
00:17:14,035 --> 00:17:14,910
Well, maybe it is old-fashioned,
but I'll fix that.

231
00:17:14,995 --> 00:17:17,872
- How do you do it?
- Wait a minute.

232
00:17:18,498 --> 00:17:21,167
There ought to be
some good ideas in here.

233
00:17:21,918 --> 00:17:23,878
This one.

234
00:17:23,962 --> 00:17:25,296
Oh, very nice. Nice.

235
00:17:25,380 --> 00:17:27,131
- Like it.
- It'll be easy.

236
00:17:27,215 --> 00:17:30,176
I'll have to shorten the sleeves,
I'll need a sash,

237
00:17:30,260 --> 00:17:33,137
- a ruffle, something for a collar...
- Cinderella!

238
00:17:33,764 --> 00:17:35,556
Oh, now what do they want?

239
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:36,974
Cinderella!

240
00:17:38,351 --> 00:17:39,518
Oh, well.

241
00:17:39,603 --> 00:17:41,562
I guess my dress will just have to wait.

242
00:17:41,646 --> 00:17:44,940
Cinderella!

243
00:17:45,025 --> 00:17:47,485
All right, all right. I'm coming.

244
00:17:50,781 --> 00:17:52,865
Poor Cinderelly.

245
00:17:52,949 --> 00:17:56,619
Every time she finds a minute,
that's the time when they begin it.

246
00:17:56,703 --> 00:17:58,621
Cinderelly, Cinderelly.

247
00:17:58,705 --> 00:18:00,498
Cinderella!

248
00:18:02,209 --> 00:18:05,544
Cinderelly, Cinderelly
Night and day it's Cinderelly

249
00:18:05,629 --> 00:18:07,588
Make the fire
Fix the breakfast

250
00:18:07,672 --> 00:18:09,465
Wash the dishes
Do the moppin'

251
00:18:09,549 --> 00:18:11,509
And the sweepin' and the dustin'

252
00:18:11,593 --> 00:18:13,302
They always keep her hoppin'

253
00:18:13,386 --> 00:18:14,845
She'd go around in circles

254
00:18:14,930 --> 00:18:16,764
Till she's very, very dizzy

255
00:18:16,848 --> 00:18:21,310
- Still they holler
- Keep her busy, Cinderelly

256
00:18:21,394 --> 00:18:23,479
Yeah. Keep her busy.

257
00:18:26,316 --> 00:18:27,983
You know what?

258
00:18:28,068 --> 00:18:31,153
- Cinderelly won't go to the ball.
- What?

259
00:18:31,238 --> 00:18:32,988
- Not go?
- What did you say?

260
00:18:33,615 --> 00:18:37,159
You'll see. They'll fix her.

261
00:18:38,286 --> 00:18:42,665
Work, work, work.
She'll never get her dress done.

262
00:18:43,250 --> 00:18:45,376
Poor Cinderelly.

263
00:18:47,212 --> 00:18:49,171
Hey! We can do it!

264
00:18:49,256 --> 00:18:51,340
We can do it
We can do it

265
00:18:51,424 --> 00:18:54,927
We can help our Cinderelly
We can make the dress so pretty

266
00:18:55,011 --> 00:18:56,762
There's nothing to it, really

267
00:18:56,847 --> 00:19:00,599
We'll tie a sash around it
Put a ribbon through it

268
00:19:00,684 --> 00:19:04,103
When dancing at the ball
she'll be more beautiful than all

269
00:19:04,187 --> 00:19:07,815
In the lovely dress
