the spell will be broken,

406
00:29:09,334 --> 00:29:11,919
and everything will be as it was before.

407
00:29:12,003 --> 00:29:14,254
Oh, I understand, but

408
00:29:14,339 --> 00:29:17,007
it's more than I ever hoped for.

409
00:29:17,091 --> 00:29:18,801
Bless you, my child.

410
00:29:18,885 --> 00:29:21,386
I... Goodness me!

411
00:29:21,471 --> 00:29:24,723
It's getting late.
Hurry up, dear. The ball can't wait.

412
00:29:24,849 --> 00:29:27,142
Have a good time.
Dance, be gay.

413
00:29:27,227 --> 00:29:29,394
Now, off you go.
You're on your way.

414
00:29:29,479 --> 00:29:31,772
With a bibbidi-bobbidi
Bibbidi-bobbidi

415
00:29:31,856 --> 00:29:33,524
Bibbidi-bobbidi-boo

416
00:30:01,427 --> 00:30:05,180
Princess Frederica
Eugenie de la Fontain.

417
00:30:09,561 --> 00:30:12,354
Mademoiselle
Augustina DuBois.

418
00:30:12,438 --> 00:30:15,858
Daughter of General Pierre DuBois.

419
00:30:26,411 --> 00:30:29,246
The boy isn't cooperating.

420
00:30:30,081 --> 00:30:34,209
Mademoiselle Leonora
Mercedes de la Tour.

421
00:30:34,294 --> 00:30:38,714
Daughter of Colonel
and Madame de la Tour.

422
00:30:45,263 --> 00:30:47,764
I can't understand it.

423
00:30:47,849 --> 00:30:50,893
There must be at least one
who'd make a suitable mother.

424
00:30:50,977 --> 00:30:52,853
Sire.

425
00:30:52,937 --> 00:30:55,397
A suitable wife.

426
00:31:14,500 --> 00:31:20,047
Mademoiselles
Drizella and Anastasia Tremaine.

427
00:31:20,131 --> 00:31:22,799
Daughters of Lady Tremaine.

428
00:31:29,098 --> 00:31:32,601
I give up.
Even I couldn't expect the boy to...

429
00:31:32,685 --> 00:31:36,229
Well, if I may say so,
Your Majesty, I did try to warn you,

430
00:31:36,314 --> 00:31:40,150
but you, Sire, are incurably romantic.

431
00:31:40,610 --> 00:31:45,197
No doubt you saw
the whole pretty picture in detail.

432
00:31:45,823 --> 00:31:49,618
The young Prince
bowing to the assembly.

433
00:31:50,411 --> 00:31:53,497
Suddenly he stops. He looks up.

434
00:31:53,581 --> 00:31:57,125
For, lo, there she stands.

435
00:31:57,627 --> 00:31:59,503
The girl of his dreams.

436
00:32:01,255 --> 00:32:03,173
Who she is or whence she came,

437
00:32:03,758 --> 00:32:06,093
he knows not, nor does he care,

438
00:32:06,177 --> 00:32:08,971
for his heart tells him that here,

439
00:32:09,055 --> 00:32:14,101
here is the maid
predestined to be his bride.

440
00:32:15,937 --> 00:32:18,605
A pretty plot for fairy tales, Sire.

441
00:32:18,690 --> 00:32:20,816
But in real life, oh, no.

442
00:32:20,900 --> 00:32:24,194
No! It was foredoomed to failure.

443
00:32:24,529 --> 00:32:27,072
Failure, eh?

444
00:32:27,156 --> 00:32:30,325
Take a look at that,
you pompous windbag.

445
00:32:31,619 --> 00:32:32,953
Who is she?

446
00:32:33,037 --> 00:32:35,122
- You know her?
- No, Sire.

447
00:32:35,206 --> 00:32:37,290
I've never seen her before.

448
00:32:37,375 --> 00:32:39,668
That's one thing in her favour.

449
00:32:39,752 --> 00:32:41,712
The waltz. Quick, the waltz!

450
00:32:45,508 --> 00:32:48,593
Lights. The lights.

451
00:33:07,572 --> 00:33:09,990
Failure, eh?

452
00:33:13,870 --> 00:33:17,330
Well... Now for a good night's sleep.

453
00:33:17,415 --> 00:33:20,125
Oh, quite so, Sire. I believe I, too...

454
00:33:20,209 --> 00:33:22,961
You will stay right here.

455
00:33:23,046 --> 00:33:26,673
See they're not disturbed,
and when the boy proposes,

456
00:33:26,758 --> 00:33:29,843
notify me immediately.

457
00:33:29,927 --> 00:33:31,386
Notify me immediately.

458
00:33:31,471 --> 00:33:33,180
And remember,

459
00:33:33,264 --> 00:33:35,766
if anything goes wrong...

460
00:33:52,075 --> 00:33:54,659
- Who is she, Mother?
- Do we know her?

461
00:33:54,744 --> 00:33:57,204
Well, the Prince certainly seems to.

462
00:33:57,288 --> 00:33:59,372
I know I've never seen her.

463
00:33:59,457 --> 00:34:00,791
Nor I.

464
00:34:00,875 --> 00:34:03,877
But she certainly is... Wait.

465
00:34:04,629 --> 00:34:07,214
There is something familiar about her.

466
00:34:17,642 --> 00:34:18,725
Ahem.

467
00:34:28,236 --> 00:34:37,244
So this is love

468
00:34:37,328 --> 00:34:41,248
So this is what makes life

469
00:34:41,332 --> 00:34:44,459
Divine

470
00:34:44,544 --> 00:34:48,046
I'm all aglow

471
00:34:48,131 --> 00:34:52,467
- And now I know
- And now I know

472
00:34:52,552 --> 00:34:57,055
The key to all Heaven

473
00:34:57,140 --> 00:35:00,600
Is mine

474
00:35:00,685 --> 00:35:04,688
My heart has wings

475
00:35:04,772 --> 00:35:08,775
And I can fly

476
00:35:08,860 --> 00:35:12,696
I'll touch every star

477
00:35:12,780 --> 00:35:16,032
In the sky

478
00:35:17,285 --> 00:35:22,164
So this is the miracle

479
00:35:22,248 --> 00:35:28,044
That I've been dreaming of

480
00:35:37,096 --> 00:35:39,514
So this

481
00:35:39,599 --> 00:35:42,225
Is

482
00:35:42,310 --> 00:35:45,729
Love

483
00:35:49,150 --> 00:35:50,734
Oh. Oh, my goodness.

484
00:35:50,818 --> 00:35:52,569
What's the matter?

485
00:35:52,653 --> 00:35:53,904
It's midnight.

486
00:35:53,988 --> 00:35:55,989
Yes, so it is. But why...

487
00:35:56,073 --> 00:35:58,366
- Goodbye.
- No, no, wait.

488
00:35:58,451 --> 00:36:01,161
- You can't go now. It's only...
- Oh, I must. Please.

489
00:36:01,245 --> 00:36:02,871
- Please, I must.
- But why?

490
00:36:02,955 --> 00:36:05,207
Well, I... Oh, the Prince,

491
00:36:05,291 --> 00:36:06,750
I haven't met the Prince.

492
00:36:06,834 --> 00:36:08,168
The Prince?

493
00:36:08,252 --> 00:36:09,377
But didn't you know...

494
00:36:10,671 --> 00:36:12,839
- Goodbye.
- No, wait.

495
00:36:12,924 --> 00:36:15,217
Come back. Please come back.

496
00:36:15,551 --> 00:36:18,136
I don't even know your name.
How will I find you?

497
00:36:18,221 --> 00:36:19,763
Wait! Please wait.

498
00:36:20,890 --> 00:36:22,224
Goodbye.

499
00:36:22,808 --> 00:36:25,060
Oh, I say. Young lady.

500
00:36:25,144 --> 00:36:28,355
- Wait!
- The Prince!

501
00:36:53,631 --> 00:36:55,090
I'm sorry.

502
00:36:55,841 --> 00:36:59,094
I guess I forgot about everything.

503
00:37:00,054 --> 00:37:01,846
Even the time, but...

504
00:37:03,307 --> 00:37:06,059
But it was so wonderful.

505
00:37:07,103 --> 00:37:09,020
And he was so handsome,

506
00:37:09,105 --> 00:37:11,523
and when we danced...

507
00:37:11,607 --> 00:37:15,235
Oh, I'm sure even the Prince
himself couldn't have been more...

508
00:37:15,319 --> 00:37:16,528
More...

509
00:37:17,696 --> 00:37:20,365
- Oh, well, it's over and...
- Cinderelly.

510
00:37:20,449 --> 00:37:22,450
Look, look! The slippers!

511
00:37:22,576 --> 00:37:23,660
Yeah, your slipper.

512
00:37:23,744 --> 00:37:25,954
Your slipper, Cinderelly.

513
00:37:30,084 --> 00:37:31,418
Thank you.

514
00:37:32,128 --> 00:37:35,046
Thank you so much, for everything.

515
00:37:44,890 --> 00:37:49,269
Your Majesty,
I see no point in beating about the bush.

516
00:37:49,353 --> 00:37:51,312
I regret to inform you, Sire,

517
00:37:51,397 --> 00:37:53,565
