524
00:38:39,487 --> 00:38:40,945
- Tell me about it.
- Well...

525
00:38:41,030 --> 00:38:43,448
- Who is she?
- I didn't get a chance...

526
00:38:43,532 --> 00:38:46,159
No matter. We've more
important things to discuss.

527
00:38:46,243 --> 00:38:47,911
Arrangements for the wedding,

528
00:38:47,995 --> 00:38:50,622
invitations, a national holiday.

529
00:38:51,332 --> 00:38:53,583
- All that sort of thing.
- But, Sire...

530
00:38:53,667 --> 00:38:56,336
Here. Have a cigar. Take a few more.

531
00:38:56,879 --> 00:38:57,921
But...

532
00:38:58,005 --> 00:39:00,798
Better practise passing these out, eh?

533
00:39:00,883 --> 00:39:04,135
But, if you'd only listen.

534
00:39:04,220 --> 00:39:05,970
And for you, my friend.

535
00:39:06,055 --> 00:39:09,807
- Your Majesty, please...
- A knighthood.

536
00:39:09,892 --> 00:39:12,393
I hereby dub you Sir...

537
00:39:13,687 --> 00:39:16,272
By the way, what title would you like?

538
00:39:16,774 --> 00:39:19,817
- Sire? She got away.
- Sir "She Got Away"?

539
00:39:19,902 --> 00:39:22,070
A peculiar title, but if that's what you...

540
00:39:22,988 --> 00:39:25,740
She what? Why, you...

541
00:39:25,866 --> 00:39:27,992
You... You traitor!

542
00:39:28,077 --> 00:39:30,995
Now, Sire.
Remember, your blood pressure.

543
00:39:31,080 --> 00:39:32,956
Treason!

544
00:39:35,793 --> 00:39:37,335
No, Sire. No!

545
00:39:37,419 --> 00:39:39,796
Sabotage!

546
00:39:40,756 --> 00:39:42,674
You were in league with the Prince.

547
00:39:42,758 --> 00:39:44,801
I tried to stop her,

548
00:39:44,885 --> 00:39:46,761
but she vanished into thin air.

549
00:39:46,845 --> 00:39:48,596
A likely story.

550
00:39:48,681 --> 00:39:52,016
But it's true, Sire.
All we could find was this glass slipper.

551
00:39:52,101 --> 00:39:54,602
The whole thing was a plot!

552
00:39:55,437 --> 00:39:58,189
But, Sire, he loves her.

553
00:39:58,274 --> 00:40:00,191
He won't rest till he finds her.

554
00:40:00,276 --> 00:40:02,193
He's determined to marry her.

555
00:40:03,571 --> 00:40:06,531
What? What did you say?

556
00:40:06,907 --> 00:40:09,492
The Prince, Sire,
swears he'll marry none

557
00:40:09,577 --> 00:40:11,703
but the girl who fits this slipper.

558
00:40:11,787 --> 00:40:13,580
He said that, did he?

559
00:40:14,623 --> 00:40:17,208
We've got him!

560
00:40:22,298 --> 00:40:25,717
But, Sire, this slipper
may fit one of any number of girls.

561
00:40:25,801 --> 00:40:28,678
That's his problem. He's given his word.

562
00:40:28,762 --> 00:40:31,889
- We'll hold him to it.
- No, Your Highness.

563
00:40:31,974 --> 00:40:33,975
I'll have nothing to do with it.

564
00:40:34,059 --> 00:40:36,769
You'll try this
on every maid in my kingdom.

565
00:40:36,854 --> 00:40:38,104
And if the shoe fits,

566
00:40:39,690 --> 00:40:41,566
bring her in.

567
00:40:41,650 --> 00:40:44,444
Yes, Your Majesty.

568
00:40:58,334 --> 00:41:00,543
Cinderella? Cinderella?

569
00:41:01,420 --> 00:41:03,713
- Cinderella! Where is that...
- Yes?

570
00:41:03,797 --> 00:41:05,131
Here I am.

571
00:41:05,674 --> 00:41:07,091
My daughters, where are they?

572
00:41:07,176 --> 00:41:08,676
I think they're still in bed.

573
00:41:10,512 --> 00:41:14,182
Don't just stand there!
Bring up the breakfast trays at once.

574
00:41:14,266 --> 00:41:15,475
And hurry!

575
00:41:16,435 --> 00:41:18,686
Wow. I wonder what's the matter.

576
00:41:18,771 --> 00:41:20,480
What's the matter with her?

577
00:41:20,564 --> 00:41:22,774
I don't know. Let's find out. Come on.

578
00:41:30,658 --> 00:41:32,784
Drizella. Drizella!

579
00:41:32,868 --> 00:41:34,994
What?

580
00:41:35,079 --> 00:41:37,038
Get up. Quick. This instant.

581
00:41:37,122 --> 00:41:38,998
We haven't a moment to lose.

582
00:41:40,209 --> 00:41:43,336
Anastasia.

583
00:41:46,090 --> 00:41:47,340
Get up, Anastasia.

584
00:41:48,467 --> 00:41:50,677
What for? Why?

585
00:41:50,761 --> 00:41:53,596
Everyone's talking about it,
the whole kingdom.

586
00:41:53,889 --> 00:41:56,182
- Hurry now. He'll be here any minute.
- Who will?

587
00:41:56,266 --> 00:41:59,310
The Grand Duke.
He's been hunting all night.

588
00:41:59,395 --> 00:42:01,479
- Hunting?
- For that girl.

589
00:42:01,563 --> 00:42:04,107
The one who lost
her slipper at the ball last night.

590
00:42:04,191 --> 00:42:06,150
They say he's madly in love with her.

591
00:42:06,235 --> 00:42:09,029
- The Duke is?
- No, no, no. The Prince!

592
00:42:09,029 --> 00:42:09,904
May we offer you some tea?

593
00:42:09,988 --> 00:42:12,573
What? Tea?

594
00:42:12,658 --> 00:42:14,951
Thank you, madam, no.

595
00:42:15,035 --> 00:42:17,620
We must proceed with the fitting.

596
00:42:17,704 --> 00:42:20,081
Of course. Anastasia, dear.

597
00:42:24,336 --> 00:42:27,129
There. I knew it was my slipper.

598
00:42:27,756 --> 00:42:29,256
Exactly my size.

599
00:42:29,341 --> 00:42:31,175
I always wear the same size.

600
00:42:31,343 --> 00:42:33,135
As soon as I saw it, I said...

601
00:42:33,220 --> 00:42:35,096
Oh, well...

602
00:42:35,180 --> 00:42:37,932
It may be a trifle snug today.

603
00:42:38,016 --> 00:42:40,601
You know how it is, dancing all night.

604
00:42:40,686 --> 00:42:42,561
I can't understand why.

605
00:42:42,646 --> 00:42:44,689
It's always fit perfectly before.

606
00:42:45,107 --> 00:42:46,983
I don't think you're half trying.

607
00:42:47,776 --> 00:42:50,111
Mother, can you...

608
00:42:50,195 --> 00:42:53,489
Quiet, my dear.
We mustn't disturb His Grace.

609
00:42:53,573 --> 00:42:57,118
Young man, are you sure
you're trying it on the right foot?

610
00:42:58,870 --> 00:43:02,623
Oh, it's the right foot, but...

611
00:43:02,708 --> 00:43:04,458
These glass shoes
aren't always reliable.

612
00:43:04,543 --> 00:43:06,460
Come on, hurry.

613
00:43:06,545 --> 00:43:08,421
Up the stairs, up the stairs!

614
00:43:10,048 --> 00:43:12,258
Lucify, Lucify.

615
00:43:15,637 --> 00:43:18,055
Up, up, up with it.

616
00:43:28,066 --> 00:43:29,233
Here.

617
00:43:45,250 --> 00:43:47,168
Why can't you hold still a minute?

618
00:43:47,252 --> 00:43:50,296
My word. Enough of this!

619
00:43:52,966 --> 00:43:55,009
The next young lady, please.

620
00:43:55,093 --> 00:43:56,719
Did you hear that, Gus?

621
00:43:56,803 --> 00:43:58,846
- Yup.
- Gotta hurry.

622
00:44:04,603 --> 00:44:06,604
Come on, come on, hurry.

623
00:44:14,154 --> 00:44:17,114
Gus-Gus, Gus-Gus, come on.

624
00:44:17,199 --> 00:44:20,034
Look, look. Just up there. Come on.

625
00:44:28,919 --> 00:44:31,087
Us is coming, Cinderelly.

626
00:44:31,171 --> 00:44:33,756
- I can get you out.
- You've got the key!

627
00:44:33,840 --> 00:44:36,759
How did you ever manage to...

628
00:44:36,843 --> 00:44:38,427
Lucifer!

629
00:44:38,512 --> 00:44:40,805
Let him go, Lucifer.

630
00:44:41,640 --> 00:44:43,432
Please, let him go.

631
00:44:44,059 --> 00:44:46,018
- Let him go.
- Let him go!

632
00:44:46,103 --> 00:44:48,562
Let him go. Let him out, you hear?

633
00:44:48,647 --> 00:44:50,397
Lucify, you...

634
00:45:28,520 --> 00:45:31,856
Bruno. Yes, Bruno!

635
00:45:32,274 --> 00:45:35,067
Quick, get Bruno. Get Bruno!

636
00:45:55,338 --> 00:45:58,549
Of all the stupid little idiots.

637
00:45:59,384 --> 00:46:01,218
I'll do it myself.

638
00:46:01,303 --> 00:46:03,012
Get away from me.

639
00:46:03,096 --> 00:46:06,140
I'll make it fit.

640
00:46:06,725 --> 00:46:08,559
- There.
- It fits.

641
00:46:08,643 --> 00:46:09,894
It fits?

642
00:46:12,063 --> 00:46:14,106
No!

643
00:46:20,155 --> 00:46:22,865
Oh, Your Grace, I'm dreadfully sorry.

644
00:46:23,241 --> 00:46:24,783
It shan't happen again.

645
00:46:24,868 --> 00:46:26,327
Precisely, madam.

646
00:46:52,604 --> 00:46:55,606
Come on, come on.
Get up, Gus-Gus, get up.

647
00:46:56,149 --> 00:46:58,108
Don't, don't, don't, don't.

648
00:46:58,777 --> 00:47:00,736
Let go, let go.

649
00:47:05,367 --> 00:47:08,452
You are the only ladies
in the household I hope... I presume.

650
00:47:08,536 --> 00:47:11,247
- There's no one else, Your Grace.
- Quite so.

651
00:47:11,331 --> 00:47:13,916
- Good day. Good day.
- Your Grace?

652
00:47:14,292 --> 00:47:17,044
Your Grace, please, wait.

653
00:47:17,128 --> 00:47:19,255
May I try it on?

654
00:47:19,339 --> 00:47:22,174
- Pay no attention.
- It's Cinderella.

655
00:47:22,259 --> 00:47:24,134
- From the kitchen.
- Ridiculous.

656
00:47:24,219 --> 00:47:26,262
She's out of her mind.

657
00:47:26,346 --> 00:47:28,264
Just an imaginative child.

658
00:47:28,348 --> 00:47:31,350
Madam,
my orders were "every maiden."

659
00:47:32,894 --> 00:47:34,436
Come, my child.

660
00:47:49,494 --> 00:47:51,370
Oh, no.

661
00:47:51,454 --> 00:47:53,914
No, no, no. Oh, no!

662
00:47:53,999 --> 00:47:56,041
Oh, this is terrible.

663
00:47:56,126 --> 00:47:58,335
The King, what will he say?

664
00:47:59,129 --> 00:48:00,587
What will he do?

665
00:48:00,672 --> 00:48:02,214
Perhaps, if it would help...

666
00:48:02,299 --> 00:48:05,718
No, no. Nothing can help now. Nothing.

667
00:48:05,844 --> 00:48:07,803
But, you see, I have the other slipper.

668
00:48:46,134 --> 00:48:48,886
Have faith in dreams

669
00:48:48,970 --> 00:48:51,680
And someday

670
00:48:51,765 --> 00:48:57,311
Your rainbow
will come smiling through

671
00:48:57,395 --> 00:49:02,191
No matter how your heart is grieving

672
00:49:02,275 --> 00:49:06,445
If you keep on believing

673
00:49:06,529 --> 00:49:09,782
The dream that you wish

674
00:49:09,866 --> 00:49:13,869
Will come true
